<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Feb 21.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Feb 21.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 02/21/97  02/14/97  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	     47.60     58.81    20.47	25.29     12.7</p>
<p>West	     69.15     73.73    26.69	28.45     33.5</p>
<p>Total Canada  116.75    132.54    23.75	26.96     23.7</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 02/21/97: 232.55 bcf, 02/14/97: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 02/21/97: 259.11 bcf, 02/14/96: 259.11 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>((--Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
